@startuml Sequence Diagram - Attendance & Certificate
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam roundCorner 15
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #34495E
    LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantFontColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
    BorderColor #F9A825
    FontSize 11
}

title <size:22><b>Academic Event Management System</b></size>\n<size:16><color:#666666>Sequence Diagram — Attendance Marking & Certificate Generation</color></size>\n
footer <size:10>Prepared for Black Book Submission | Academic Event Management System</size>

actor "<b>Student</b>" as Student
actor "<b>Admin</b>" as Admin
participant "<b>ParticipantsList</b>\n(Admin Page)" as PL
participant "<b>RegistrationController</b>\n(/api/registrations)" as RC
participant "<b>RegistrationService</b>" as RS
participant "<b>CertificateController</b>\n(/api/certificates)" as CC
participant "<b>CertificateService</b>" as CS
participant "<b>CertificatePdfService</b>\n(iTextPDF)" as CPS
participant "<b>NotificationService</b>" as NS
participant "<b>EmailService</b>\n(@Async)" as ES
database "<b>PostgreSQL</b>" as DB

== Phase 1: Admin Views Participants List ==

Admin -> PL : Navigate to Participants\nfor Event #3
activate PL
PL -> RC : **GET** /api/registrations/event/3
activate RC
RC -> DB : findByEventId(3)\nJOIN fetch user, event
activate DB
DB --> RC : List<Registration>\n(45 participants)
deactivate DB
RC --> PL : Participants JSON\nwith user details
deactivate RC
PL --> Admin : Display table:\n| Name | Status | Payment | Attendance |\n| Jay Patel | Approved | SUCCESS | Not Marked |
deactivate PL

== Phase 2: Admin Marks Attendance ==

Admin -> PL : Click **"Present"** button\nfor Student #5 (Jay Patel)
activate PL
PL -> RC : **PUT** /api/registrations/attendance/12/Present
activate RC

RC -> RS : markAttendance(12, "Present")
activate RS

RS -> DB : findById(12)
activate DB
DB --> RS : Registration object
deactivate DB

RS -> RS : Validate:\n• Registration must exist\n• Status must be Approved

RS -> DB : save(registration)\nattendanceStatus = "Present"
activate DB
DB --> RS : Updated Registration
deactivate DB

RS --> RC : Updated Registration
deactivate RS
RC --> PL : **200 OK**
deactivate RC

PL -> PL : Refresh participants table
PL --> Admin : Student now shows\n"Present" in Attendance column ✅
deactivate PL

== Phase 3: Admin Generates Certificate ==

Admin -> PL : Click **"Generate Certificate"**\nfor Jay Patel (Registration #12)
activate PL
PL -> CC : **POST** /api/certificates/generate/12
activate CC

CC -> CS : generateCertificate(12)
activate CS

CS -> DB : findByRegistrationId(12)
activate DB
DB --> CS : Optional.empty()\n<b>No duplicate certificate</b>
deactivate DB

CS -> DB : findById(12)
activate DB
DB --> CS : Registration\n(status=Approved, attendance=Present)
deactivate DB

CS -> CS : Validate eligibility:\n✓ status = Approved\n✓ attendance = Present

CS -> CS : Generate certificateNumber\n"CERT-1725559200"

CS -> DB : save(Certificate)\nissueDate = today
activate DB
DB --> CS : Saved Certificate\n(id = 7)
deactivate DB

CS -> NS : createNotification(student,\n"Certificate Generated",\n"CERTIFICATE")
activate NS
NS -> DB : save(Notification)
activate DB
DB --> NS : Saved
deactivate DB
deactivate NS

CS -> ES : sendCertificateNotification(\nstudent, "CERT-1725559200")\n<b>@Async</b>
activate ES
ES --> CS : (email queued)
deactivate ES

CS --> CC : Certificate\n(id=7, number="CERT-1725559200")
deactivate CS
CC --> PL : **200 OK**
deactivate CC
PL --> Admin : "Certificate Generated!" ✅
deactivate PL

== Phase 4: Student Downloads Certificate ==

Student -> PL : Navigate to\n"My Certificates" page
activate PL
PL -> CC : **GET** /api/certificates/download/12
activate CC

CC -> CS : getByRegistration(12)
activate CS
CS -> DB : findByRegistrationId(12)
activate DB
DB --> CS : Certificate object
deactivate DB
CS --> CC : Certificate
deactivate CS

CC -> CPS : generateCertificate(certificate)
activate CPS

note over CPS
  <b>CertificatePdfService — PDF Generation Pipeline:</b>
  
  <b>Step 1:</b> Determine event category from Event → EventCategory
  
  <b>Step 2:</b> Load category-themed background:
  • bg_workshop.png (for Workshops)
  • bg_technical.png (for Technical events)
  • bg_seminar.png (for Seminars)
  • bg_cultural.png (for Cultural events)
  • bg_hackathon.png (for Hackathons)
  
  <b>Step 3:</b> Load college_logo.png
  Remove white background (make transparent)
  
  <b>Step 4:</b> Overlay text elements:
  • "Certificate of Completion" (title)
  • "This is to certify that" (italic)
  • Student full name (large, bold)
  • Event title
  • Event date + Issue date
  
  <b>Step 5:</b> Draw handwritten signature image
end note

CPS -> CPS : Load background PNG\nbased on event category

CPS -> CPS : Load college_logo.png\nRemove white background

CPS -> CPS : Draw text:\n• Title (centered)\n• Student name (large)\n• Event name\n• Date\n• Signature

CPS --> CC : byte[] (PDF binary data)
deactivate CPS

CC --> PL : **200 OK**\n`Content-Type: application/pdf`
deactivate CC

PL -> PL : Trigger browser download\n"CERT-1725559200.pdf"
PL --> Student : PDF downloaded ✅
deactivate PL

note over Student, DB
  <b>Attendance & Certificate Summary:</b>
  
  <b>Attendance Flow:</b>
  • Admin views participants list (filtered by event)
  • Clicks "Present" / "Absent" for each student
  • Backend updates attendanceStatus on Registration
  • Only Approved registrations can be marked
  
  <b>Certificate Flow:</b>
  • Admin triggers generation (validates eligibility)
  • Certificate number: "CERT-{timestamp}" (unique)
  • PDF generated with iTextPDF 5.5.13.3
  • Category-specific backgrounds (5 types)
  • College logo + handwritten signature overlay
  • Student downloads PDF from "My Certificates"
  • Notification + email sent asynchronously
end note

@enduml
